post.description:
Set agent scope for out_of_scope detection.

Body:
{
    "in_scope": "What the agent should handle",
    "out_of_scope": "What the agent should NOT handle"
}

Bulk import intents from file or JSON.

Accepts:
- File upload (CSV/JSON)
- JSON body with intents array

CSV format:
intent_id,name,description,keywords
greet,Greeting,User says hello,"hi,hello,hey"

JSON format:
{
    "intents": [
        {"intent_id": "greet", "name": "Greeting", "description": "User says hello", "keywords": ["hi", "hello"]}
    ]
}

Run evaluation asynchronously via Cloud Run Job.

This endpoint has been converted to async-by-default to eliminate Cloud Run
request timeouts. All runs are now enqueued as Cloud Run Jobs and return
immediately with a job_id for polling.

Returns: 202 + {job_id, status, total_rows, execution}
Poll status via: GET /api/evaluation/run/status/{job_id}
Retrieve results via: GET /api/evaluation/run/result/{job_id}

Test the chatbot connection with a sample query.

Body:
{
    "query": "Hello, how are you?",
    "agent_id": "..." (optional)
}

patch.description:
Persist human-review selections and comments for an evaluation.

The data is stored inside the evaluation history JSON in GCS so it
survives reloads and is available across devices.

Body:
{
    "agent_name": "MyAgent",
    "reviews": {
        "<rowKey>": {
            "human_review": "acceptable" | "not-acceptable",
            "comment": "free-text"
        },
        ...
    }
}

put.description:
Update human review for a specific query result.

Body:
{
    "review": "Correct" | "Incorrect" | "Needs Investigation" | "Override: Acceptable"
}

get.description:
Get the scope definition for an agent.

Returns:
    {
        "in_scope": "energy contracts, bills, SMART APP...",
        "out_of_scope": "games, sports, weather..."
    }
